  "id": "cesamet",
  "term": "Cesamet",
  "definition": "Cesamet is nabilone, a synthetic cannabinoid related to dibenzopyrane that is used to reduce nausea and vomiting. Its exact action is not fully understood, but it is thought to strongly activate CB1 and CB2 cannabinoid receptors, with CB1 activity linked to less chemotherapy-related nausea.",
